From 83a78c5ba40a104f677211cf7aaccb64f2b5c2c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yo'av Moshe <github@yoavmoshe.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:18:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] arm64: mt8163-douglas: mainline port of the Amazon Fire
 HD 8 (2017)

Built-in device tree for douglas (LK's FDT is unusable), NT35521 DSI panel,
MT8163 thermal with DT-provided calibration words, cpufreq OPPs with the
SY8827N external buck, MT6323 PMIC keys/RTC, watchdog suspend fix, and the
m4u node disabled until a real IOMMU setup exists. Also a no-op quirk file
with a watchdog-register guard for risky boot-time register experiments.

See HANDOFF.md in the bjesus/firehd8-pmos repository for the full story.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
