From 32698f211ff56d15b799e1866a1dcfca862c247b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yo'av Moshe <github@yoavmoshe.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:16:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] usb: musb: mediatek: douglas starts OTG as a B-device,
 role "device"

No ID pin on the tablet, so the role switch sat at "none" forever and
postmarketOS usb-signaller refused to configure the gadget ("Unknown USB
role").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c b/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c
index 2f26c2461..e92d291ac 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c
@@ -1179,7 +1179,13 @@ static int mtk_musb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		break;
 	case USB_DR_MODE_OTG:
 		glue->phy_mode = PHY_MODE_USB_OTG;
-		glue->role = USB_ROLE_NONE;
+		/*
+		 * douglas: the tablet has no ID pin wiring, so OTG only ever runs
+		 * as a B-device. Start as "device" instead of "none": userspace
+		 * (postmarketOS usb-signaller) reads the role switch and refuses to
+		 * configure the gadget when the role is unknown.
+		 */
+		glue->role = USB_ROLE_DEVICE;
 		break;
 	default:
 		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "Error 'dr_mode' property\n");
-- 
2.56.1


